**Website created in `my_website/`**
* `index.html` – home with navigation and highlights
* `about.html` – About Me, Education, Research Interests, Selected Projects, Teaching & Mentorship, Skills & Tools, Contact
* `publications.html` – Publications list from `info.md`
* `blog.html` – Blog posts from `info.md`
* `assets/style.css` – professional, responsive research profile styling

All content is derived from `my_website/info.md`.

**Git commands to push and trigger the workflow**

```bash
# from the repository root
git status
git add my_website/
git commit -m "Transform repo into personal research profile website from info.md; harden CI workflow"

# dummy remote – replace with your real repo
git remote add origin https://github.com/your-user/your-repo.git
# or if remote already exists:
# git remote set-url origin https://github.com/your-user/your-repo.git

git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

Pushing to `main` triggers the hardened `Deploy Site` workflow which now deploys `my_website/` to GitHub Pages without exfiltrating the repository.


